# Log in to the Treechat app and look around, on a real phone. The account
# comes from the environment (or ./.env): TREECHAT_EMAIL, TREECHAT_PASSWORD.
# Never write credentials in a scenario; results show the ${...} placeholder.
# Use a dedicated test account. Read-only once logged in: never posts or
# upvalues.
#   jevb run examples/login-treechat-app.jevb --device "pixel 9" --app treechat.apk
open
act? dismiss the notifications permission prompt without allowing
check is this a login page?
type the email field => ${TREECHAT_EMAIL}
type the password field => ${TREECHAT_PASSWORD}
press HideKeyboard
act log in
refute is an error or "wrong password" message shown?
check is the user logged in, with a stream of posts shown?
act open the sidebar menu
act open the Channels page
check is a list of channels shown?
